Name: unregisterVoiceCommand

Type: command

Syntax: unregisterVoiceCommand <phrase>

Summary:
Removes a previously registered voice command phrase. The phrase will no
longer be recognised by the speech recognition engine.

Introduced: 1.1.0

OS: mac

Platforms: desktop

Example:
-- Remove a single phrase
unregisterVoiceCommand "open stack"

Example:
-- Dynamically remove commands that are no longer applicable
repeat for each element tCmd in tDisabledCommands
    unregisterVoiceCommand tCmd
end repeat

Parameters:
phrase (string): The exact phrase (case-insensitive) to unregister. If
the phrase is not currently registered, the command is a no-op.

Description:
Use <unregisterVoiceCommand> to remove a phrase that was previously
added with <registerVoiceCommand>. After this call the speech recognition
engine will no longer match that phrase, and no <voiceCommand> message
will be fired for it.

If the phrase is not found in the registry the command succeeds silently
with no error.

To remove all registered phrases at once, use <unregisterAllVoiceCommands>.

References: registerVoiceCommand (command), unregisterAllVoiceCommands (command),
startListening (command), voiceCommand (message)

Tags: speech, voice
